+// browsception: WebKit repaints a renderer in full whenever it re-lays itself
+// out (LayoutRepainter's selfNeedsLayout() test, and the NeedsFullRepaint layer
+// bit set by setNeedsLayout below). That blanket repaint exists to cover
+// reflowed INLINE content: RenderText has no repaint pass of its own, and the
+// containing block's repaint is what covers moved text (see
+// setFullRepaintOnParentInlineBoxLayerIfNeeded in RenderBlockFlow.cpp). For a
+// block container whose children are all block-level the protection is
+// redundant — every child repaints itself, either from its own layout()
+// (LayoutRepainter), from the layer-position pass, or, when it moves without
+// needing layout, from repaintDuringLayoutIfMoved (which we make unconditional
+// for the container types allowed here). The container's own painting
+// (background/border/outline) is still covered: with the full bit off,
+// repaintAfterLayoutIfNeeded diffs old and new rects and repaints the deltas,
+// including a full repaint when bounds move or decorations scale with size.
+//
+// Excluded because the container paints something spanning its children, which
+// only its own repaint covers: fieldsets (border gap around the legend),
+// multicolumn flows (column rules), tables and their parts (collapsed borders),
+// and the RenderView (document background propagation, full-page relayout).
+bool RenderObject::blockLevelChildrenIssueOwnRepaints() const
+{
+    if (isRenderView() || isTablePart() || isRenderTable())
+        return false;
+    if (auto* blockFlow = dynamicDowncast<RenderBlockFlow>(*this))
+        return !blockFlow->childrenInline() && !blockFlow->isFieldset() && !blockFlow->multiColumnFlow() && !blockFlow->isRenderFragmentedFlow();
+    if (is<RenderGrid>(*this) || is<RenderFlexibleBox>(*this))
+        return !downcast<RenderBlock>(*this).childrenInline();
+    return false;
